'haut-bailly|2018':{blend:{CS:55,ME:35,CF:5,PV:5},src:'technical-sheet-vintage-2018-hautbailly.pdf',note:'From December 2017 to May 2018, Bordeaux had 800 mm of rain, the equivalent of an entire year of rainfall. Spring was cold and the vintage started late. June was hot and humid! A virulent mildew threatened the entire French vineyard. This pressure extended until early August. Unfortunately our vineyard was not spared. Mid-July, the same day that France won the football World Cup, the trend of the vintage was reversed. Summer was dry and hot (the hottest since 2003 and 1947). The speed of the vine growth was rapid and the water sufficiency stimulated the enlargement of the berries. These conditions made it possible to make up the vegetative delay of spring. The vintage was earlier than initially expected.'},
